// Strings: concatenation and equality. The word-kernel only handles scalars, so
// string operands fall back to the tree-walker — and both must agree.

#[test]
fn concat() ( assert_eq("hello" ++ " world", "hello world") )

#[test]
fn equality() ( assert("hi" == "hi") )

// NOTE: string *methods* (`.len()`, `.slice(…)`) are `ExprKind::Invoke`, which the
// tree-walker doesn't handle yet ("indirect calls not yet supported"). Those
// cases from the old suite are parked until the evaluator grows native methods.
